1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,313
Your crew has spent this whole class on the bridge.

2
00:00:05,113 --> 00:00:06,940
Today they get up,

3
00:00:07,390 --> 00:00:09,319
and they leave the ship, twice over.

4
00:00:11,119 --> 00:00:14,232
Once into a place made of rooms and choices.

5
00:00:15,132 --> 00:00:17,153
And once onto a map they walk across.

6
00:00:18,953 --> 00:00:22,274
And both of them hang on one line of a landmark.

7
00:00:23,474 --> 00:00:26,274
Here's a station, like the ones you've written before.

8
00:00:27,174 --> 00:00:28,441
It's in the home system,

9
00:00:28,891 --> 00:00:31,468
so nobody has to fly anywhere.

10
00:00:33,268 --> 00:00:35,048
And it has one new line.

11
00:00:35,498 --> 00:00:37,643
Site, and a key.

12
00:00:39,443 --> 00:00:41,756
That line says the crew can leave the ship here.

13
00:00:42,656 --> 00:00:44,787
And the key is the name of a file.

14
00:00:45,237 --> 00:00:47,254
Customs, dot a m d.

15
00:00:48,454 --> 00:00:49,762
So I make that file,

16
00:00:50,212 --> 00:00:51,692
and the whole place goes in it.

17
00:00:53,492 --> 00:00:54,771
It has three chapters in it.

18
00:00:55,671 --> 00:00:57,431
Voices says who's talking.

19
00:00:58,331 --> 00:01:00,282
Hails is the call that comes when we dock.

20
00:01:02,082 --> 00:01:02,919
Look at this answer.

21
00:01:03,819 --> 00:01:07,873
After it comes a semicolon, the word signal, and boarding down.

22
00:01:08,773 --> 00:01:10,402
That's the game's own word,

23
00:01:10,852 --> 00:01:12,820
and it's what sends a party.

24
00:01:14,620 --> 00:01:15,643
Then come the rooms,

25
00:01:16,093 --> 00:01:18,400
and the first one is where they arrive.

26
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:20,929
Every room has a way back,

27
00:01:21,379 --> 00:01:23,349
and every room has a way home.

28
00:01:24,549 --> 00:01:27,144
Two more things on this one answer.

29
00:01:28,944 --> 00:01:30,926
The first is learn the manifest.

30
00:01:31,826 --> 00:01:33,465
Now the party knows a fact,

31
00:01:33,915 --> 00:01:35,017
and the place keeps it.

32
00:01:35,917 --> 00:01:38,545
This line is only spoken before they know it,

33
00:01:38,995 --> 00:01:40,458
and this one only after.

34
00:01:42,258 --> 00:01:44,594
And then signal, manifest read.

35
00:01:45,494 --> 00:01:46,930
That word is mine.

36
00:01:47,830 --> 00:01:50,752
Over in the universe file, I add a step of story

37
00:01:51,202 --> 00:01:54,726
that's done when it hears that same word.

38
00:01:56,526 --> 00:01:58,706
That's how a place finishes a step.

39
00:02:00,506 --> 00:02:05,099
Its briefing opens with the Customs House itself, drawn beside the words.

40
00:02:05,999 --> 00:02:09,007
It's the same model as the landmark's Art line,

41
00:02:09,457 --> 00:02:12,115
so the crew sees where they're going.

42
00:02:13,315 --> 00:02:15,475
Lint first, and it's clean.

43
00:02:16,375 --> 00:02:17,651
There are seven files now,

44
00:02:18,101 --> 00:02:20,491
and it read the new one with the rest.

45
00:02:22,291 --> 00:02:25,754
It knows boarding down is the game's own word.

46
00:02:26,654 --> 00:02:29,276
And it found my signal at both ends,

47
00:02:29,726 --> 00:02:32,357
the answer in one file and the step in the other.

48
00:02:34,157 --> 00:02:35,241
Now let's dock with it.

49
00:02:36,141 --> 00:02:38,344
A call comes in from the Customs House.

50
00:02:39,244 --> 00:02:41,950
Comms answers, and sends a party.

51
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:43,841
And here's the counter.

52
00:02:45,641 --> 00:02:46,890
I read the manifest,

53
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,534
and the step is done and paid.

54
00:02:50,434 --> 00:02:51,326
Back at the counter,

55
00:02:51,776 --> 00:02:54,073
the clerk has a different line for me now.

56
00:02:55,273 --> 00:02:57,627
Now the second place, and here's the rule for it.

57
00:02:58,527 --> 00:02:59,385
Say it with me.

58
00:03:01,185 --> 00:03:03,521
The landmark says site, tally yard.

59
00:03:04,421 --> 00:03:07,344
The map's first line says area, tally yard.

60
00:03:08,244 --> 00:03:09,474
It's the same key,

61
00:03:09,924 --> 00:03:11,544
and nothing else joins them.

62
00:03:13,344 --> 00:03:14,744
A map needs pictures,

63
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:17,070
and they come in two art packs.

64
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:21,760
So I add two lines to story dot json,

65
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:23,411
and I watch my commas.

66
00:03:24,311 --> 00:03:26,302
One line at the end of the settings file.

67
00:03:27,202 --> 00:03:29,154
And then I fetch them, once.

68
00:03:30,354 --> 00:03:32,446
I'm handing you this map finished,

69
00:03:32,896 --> 00:03:35,360
because drawing one is a class of its own.

70
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:38,417
Read it as a picture.

71
00:03:39,317 --> 00:03:41,030
There's a landing pad on the left,

72
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,392
and a walled house with one door.

73
00:03:45,192 --> 00:03:48,017
And there's the first line, area, tally yard.

74
00:03:49,817 --> 00:03:51,400
Then the site's own file.

75
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:53,922
It has the same call as before.

76
00:03:54,822 --> 00:03:56,691
And then what stands on the map.

77
00:03:57,141 --> 00:03:59,873
A door, a keycard, a terminal, a ledger.

78
00:04:00,773 --> 00:04:02,156
A calm man to talk to,

79
00:04:02,606 --> 00:04:04,802
and a loader that attacks.

80
00:04:06,602 --> 00:04:08,683
Every key starts with the word yard.

81
00:04:09,583 --> 00:04:12,647
Keep to that, and two places can never share a key.

82
00:04:13,847 --> 00:04:16,461
One more landmark, with its one line.

83
00:04:17,361 --> 00:04:18,533
One more step of story,

84
00:04:18,983 --> 00:04:20,143
opened by the first one.

85
00:04:21,943 --> 00:04:24,791
And lint says clean, for all eight files.

86
00:04:25,691 --> 00:04:27,075
It reads the map as well.

87
00:04:28,875 --> 00:04:31,820
Change the map's first line to some other word,

88
00:04:32,270 --> 00:04:34,809
and lint tells you the site will not exist.

89
00:04:35,709 --> 00:04:37,632
The game's log says the same.

90
00:04:38,832 --> 00:04:40,323
So we dock with the yard,

91
00:04:40,773 --> 00:04:42,003
and the call comes.

92
00:04:42,903 --> 00:04:44,522
I go down from Weapons,

93
00:04:44,972 --> 00:04:46,898
and the side story is mine.

94
00:04:48,698 --> 00:04:50,418
First I deal with the loader.

95
00:04:51,318 --> 00:04:52,362
Then I try the door,

96
00:04:52,812 --> 00:04:54,955
and it stays shut.

97
00:04:55,855 --> 00:04:57,688
The keycard's lying out in the yard.

98
00:04:58,588 --> 00:05:00,839
I pick it up, and now the door opens.

99
00:05:02,639 --> 00:05:04,094
Inside there's the ledger.

100
00:05:04,994 --> 00:05:07,353
I close it, and the short count is done and paid.

101
00:05:09,153 --> 00:05:11,158
And when the last of us beams up,

102
00:05:11,608 --> 00:05:12,968
the visit is over.

103
00:05:14,168 --> 00:05:16,467
Now I dock again, and go back down.

104
00:05:17,367 --> 00:05:18,543
The door's still open,

105
00:05:18,993 --> 00:05:20,270
and the loader's still down.

106
00:05:22,070 --> 00:05:24,178
I leave the system, and I come back.

107
00:05:25,078 --> 00:05:26,827
The game built that station new,

108
00:05:27,277 --> 00:05:29,241
and the yard is just as I left it.

109
00:05:31,041 --> 00:05:33,408
Then I close the game, and continue.

110
00:05:33,858 --> 00:05:35,041
It's the same again.

111
00:05:36,841 --> 00:05:38,613
And here it is in the save.

112
00:05:39,063 --> 00:05:41,174
The door, the keycard, the loader,

113
00:05:41,624 --> 00:05:44,097
and what we learned in each place.

114
00:05:45,297 --> 00:05:47,210
Two honest words before you go.

115
00:05:49,010 --> 00:05:51,690
When I checked this page, a script did all of it,

116
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:54,097
and nobody was watching a screen.

117
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,620
And always give a site a call.

118
00:05:58,520 --> 00:06:01,574
A place with no call opens the moment you dock,

119
00:06:02,024 --> 00:06:03,746
and nobody asked the crew first.

120
00:06:04,646 --> 00:06:06,777
If they cast off without going down,

121
00:06:07,227 --> 00:06:08,756
that visit just ends.

122
00:06:10,556 --> 00:06:11,558
Now it's your turn.

123
00:06:12,458 --> 00:06:14,006
Rename the customs house,

124
00:06:14,456 --> 00:06:15,954
and give it a fifth room.

125
00:06:16,854 --> 00:06:19,581
Then walk the yard as far as the ledger.
